{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1514020-ix-pronunciation","id":1514020,"title":"IX Pronunciation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Anima"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-06T09:55:39-07:00","id":1514020,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> IX Pronunciation","content":"Maybe this is covered in the manuscript and I just missed it, but how is this intended to be pronunced? I see 4 possiblities:<br /> 1. as the number &quot;nine.&quot; <br /> 2. as the letters &quot;eye ecks.&quot;<br /> 3. as a word &quot;icks.&quot;<br /> 4. as numbers separately &quot;one ten&quot;<br /> <br /> Of that list 2 and 3 seem most likely to me. How are you all handling it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T13:04:18-07:00","id":1514043,"title":"","content":"Since both letters are capitalized and they're taken from the names of the heads, I suspect &quot;eye ecks&quot; is correct. Kind of like KFC, IBM, or CBS.<br /> <br /> edit: Weird. Don't know why the forum spontaneously changed my answer to &quot;Onyx Path&quot; in link format.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 06-07-2023, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/